# Data artifacts must be byte-identical on every platform, because committed manifests record their
# sha256 and CI (Linux) verifies it. With core.autocrlf=true and no rule here, git stores LF but
# checks out CRLF on Windows, so a checksum computed on one platform fails on the other.
# Deterministic LF for line-oriented data keeps a Windows generation and a Linux CI run in agreement.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
